# Copy to .lkmabt.env and fill locally. Never commit the copy.
# Provider commands read .lkmabt.env from the working directory automatically
# when it exists; a missing default file is fine. Pass --env-file <path> only to
# use a different file. cleanup reads no env file.
# Cluster selection lives in .lkmabt-clusters.yaml; this file holds provider
# credentials only. Values in the process environment take precedence over
# this file.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN and GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN are optional. Leave either empty to
# authenticate at run time: GitHub runs the gh browser login; GitLab opens the
# personal access token page and prompts for the token without echo. Interactive
# GitLab entry is limited to gitlab.com; set GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN for any other
# endpoint. GitLab tokens need the api and write_repository scopes, and PaC
# rejects OAuth tokens.
#
# A configured GITHUB_TOKEN needs the repo and read:org scopes, push access to
# the fixture repository, and an owner who administers redhat-appstudio-qe to
# list App installations. Classic or OAuth tokens may also need read:user to
# list App installations limited to selected repositories
# (gh auth refresh -h github.com -s read:user). In a terminal, a token that
# fails these checks falls back to an existing gh login when it passes them,
# then to the gh browser login.
#
# LKMABT keeps acquired credentials in a private temporary directory and
# deletes it when the run ends; a GitLab token it acquired is revoked once
# after the last cluster. A configured GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN is never revoked.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN=
GITLAB_API_URL=https://gitlab.com/api/v4
